### p4. what a const generic width surface carries on the pinned nightly
### the bar is the ungated column: `the_unstable_machinery_does_not_reach_a_consumer`

arm  what                                                 ungated cc  ungated bld gated    
A1   const generic as a value in a body (baseline)        compiles    compiles    compiles 
A2   arithmetic on const widths in a TYPE position: N<{W + F}> REFUSED     REFUSED     compiles 
A3   comparison of const widths in a where clause: W >= F REFUSED     REFUSED     compiles 
A4   arithmetic in an associated const, used as a value   compiles    compiles    compiles 
A5   an associated const used as a const generic argument REFUSED     REFUSED     compiles 
A6   a consumer-facing alias fixing the const (option 5's shape) compiles    compiles    compiles 
A7   a const assertion in an associated const (option 7's shape) compiles    compiles    compiles 
C5   option 7's assertion on a VIOLATING width (must be refused) compiles    REFUSED     REFUSED  
C4   a deliberately broken arm (must fail in both columns) REFUSED     REFUSED     REFUSED  

  `ungated cc` is `--emit metadata`, what `cargo check` runs.
  `ungated bld` is `--emit link`, what `cargo build` runs.
  a row differing between them is a check a consumer's `cargo check` misses.

CONTROLS
  C1  the baseline compiles ungated                  as required  required=compiles
  C2  some arm is refused ungated                    as required  required=a refusal
  C3  some ungated refusal is rescued by the gate    as required  required=rescued
  C4  the broken arm fails in both columns           as required  required=refused twice
  C5  option 7's assertion refuses a violating width as required  required=refused twice
  C5b it is refused under codegen specifically       as required  required=refused

THE FIRST DIAGNOSTIC OF EACH UNGATED REFUSAL
  A2   error: generic parameters may not be used in const operations
  A3   error: generic parameters may not be used in const operations
  A5   error: generic parameters may not be used in const operations
  C5   error[E0080]: evaluation panicked: declared width is narrower than its fraction
  C4   error[E0425]: cannot find function `this_function_does_not_exist` in this scope

THE EMISSION SPLIT, WHICH IS THE PART A DESIGN HAS TO KNOW
  C5   `cargo check` accepts, `cargo build` refuses

WHAT A CONSUMER MAY WRITE WITH NO FEATURE OF ITS OWN
  A1   const generic as a value in a body (baseline)
  A4   arithmetic in an associated const, used as a value
  A6   a consumer-facing alias fixing the const (option 5's shape)
  A7   a const assertion in an associated const (option 7's shape)

